WEBVTT

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:45.400
(Support Admin Watch on kissFlix.co)

00:00:47.777 --> 00:00:51.072
THE APARTMENT JOB

00:00:52.156 --> 00:00:54.075
I happened to be there

00:00:55.326 --> 00:00:57.745
in his final moments.

00:01:00.123 --> 00:01:02.250
Why did you do it?

00:01:02.333 --> 00:01:04.752
You should have been there for him

00:01:05.420 --> 00:01:07.714
when he passed away.

00:01:09.299 --> 00:01:11.384
But don't worry.

00:01:12.385 --> 00:01:14.721
He didn't suffer when he passed.

00:01:16.264 --> 00:01:17.265
You…

00:01:21.144 --> 00:01:22.437
What did you do?

00:01:26.316 --> 00:01:27.150
Huh?

00:01:32.488 --> 00:01:34.032
Remember how I said

00:01:34.616 --> 00:01:36.951
hangnails should be ripped off,
even if you bleed?

00:01:38.328 --> 00:01:40.788
He seemed to be a hangnail

00:01:40.872 --> 00:01:43.583
in your life.

00:01:44.626 --> 00:01:47.795
So I ripped it off for you.

00:01:49.088 --> 00:01:50.924
Don't you feel relieved now?

00:01:56.471 --> 00:01:58.556
I offer my deepest

00:02:00.016 --> 00:02:01.309
condolences.

00:02:14.239 --> 00:02:15.073
Well then…

00:02:44.435 --> 00:02:45.645
Mr. Kim!

00:02:46.187 --> 00:02:48.106
Don't make a scene and come here.

00:02:50.024 --> 00:02:51.985
You're not some thug.

00:02:55.446 --> 00:02:57.865
The chief mourner shouldn't step out.

00:02:58.449 --> 00:03:00.159
You should keep your old boss company.

00:03:03.538 --> 00:03:05.873
You're the hangnail in my life.

00:03:06.708 --> 00:03:08.543
I'll rip you off myself,

00:03:09.085 --> 00:03:12.130
whether I bleed
or tear my own flesh as well.

00:03:13.089 --> 00:03:14.298
I'll make sure

00:03:15.383 --> 00:03:17.260
you feel the pain.

00:03:18.344 --> 00:03:20.054
I'll look forward to it.

00:03:21.139 --> 00:03:25.018
But be careful not to rip
your whole nail off.

00:03:25.601 --> 00:03:26.811
That pain

00:03:26.894 --> 00:03:29.147
will last forever.

00:04:09.562 --> 00:04:10.772
Move.

00:04:10.855 --> 00:04:11.981
Where are you going?

00:04:13.316 --> 00:04:15.151
Will you go and kill Lee Chung-won?

00:04:16.027 --> 00:04:17.528
Yong-man just died.

00:04:18.863 --> 00:04:21.532
He died because of me.

00:04:22.617 --> 00:04:25.620
And you expect me to just stay here,
bowing to him?

00:04:29.624 --> 00:04:32.543
You're not going to seek revenge.

00:04:32.627 --> 00:04:34.504
You're running away from guilt.

00:04:37.507 --> 00:04:38.633
What?

00:04:39.425 --> 00:04:40.635
Mr. Park.

00:04:41.552 --> 00:04:43.971
You don't even have the guts
to look at his photo.

00:04:44.055 --> 00:04:46.516
You're a coward running away
by using revenge as an excuse.

00:04:46.599 --> 00:04:47.809
Isn't that right?

00:04:48.559 --> 00:04:49.811
Going out there and dying

00:04:49.894 --> 00:04:52.021
is less scary
than staying here and crying,

00:04:52.772 --> 00:04:53.689
isn't it?

00:04:56.901 --> 00:04:59.737
What the hell do you know
about how I feel?

00:05:00.696 --> 00:05:03.574
I feel like my heart's going to burst!

00:05:04.367 --> 00:05:06.202
What am I supposed to do?

00:05:06.786 --> 00:05:08.621
What should I do, then?

00:05:16.879 --> 00:05:18.506
Just cry, Mr. Park.

00:05:19.841 --> 00:05:22.510
If you have the guts to die,
just stay here and cry,

00:05:23.261 --> 00:05:25.263
and face Lee Chung-won after that.

00:05:27.432 --> 00:05:30.935
Then you'll be able to see
what Lee Chung-won fears the most.

00:05:36.023 --> 00:05:36.858
I…

00:05:48.327 --> 00:05:49.704
Go tell your old boss

00:05:50.329 --> 00:05:53.082
that you're grateful
he treated you like his own son

00:05:54.542 --> 00:05:56.794
and that you'll avenge him,

00:05:56.878 --> 00:05:58.713
no matter what it takes.

00:06:22.320 --> 00:06:25.990
SONS: PARK HAE-KANG, KIM GYEONG-NAM,
JANG JE-GIL, KIM DOONG-HUI

00:06:27.074 --> 00:06:31.871
THE APARTMENT JOB

00:06:36.209 --> 00:06:38.502
Why are you drinking so much?

00:06:40.713 --> 00:06:43.633
How many bottles have you had?
You're all drunk.

00:06:43.716 --> 00:06:45.218
Stop drinking!

00:06:45.301 --> 00:06:46.719
I'm not giving you any more.

00:06:46.802 --> 00:06:48.679
Just one more bottle, please.

00:06:49.305 --> 00:06:50.556
Just one more.

00:06:50.640 --> 00:06:52.767
This is the last one, okay?

00:06:53.684 --> 00:06:54.769
Excuse me!

00:06:55.686 --> 00:06:58.856
The table with the bald guy.

00:06:58.940 --> 00:07:00.358
-One bottle of soju.
-Okay.

00:07:00.983 --> 00:07:02.693
Thank you for coming.

00:07:02.777 --> 00:07:04.320
-Of course.
-Of course, we should come.

00:07:04.403 --> 00:07:06.489
-Of course.
-Tell me if you need anything.

00:07:09.158 --> 00:07:12.328
Big Guy, stop eating, will you?

00:07:12.411 --> 00:07:16.207
I'm so sad,
but I can't help feeling hungry.

00:07:16.290 --> 00:07:18.000
Eat as much as you want.

00:07:18.084 --> 00:07:20.127
You sure know how to eat. Oh, hello.

00:07:22.922 --> 00:07:24.340
-Chew thoroughly.
-Okay.

00:07:44.277 --> 00:07:45.486
Mr. Park.

00:07:46.320 --> 00:07:49.657
Do you know who's the scariest
in a gambling den?

00:07:50.658 --> 00:07:52.493
The one who has nothing to lose?

00:07:53.744 --> 00:07:54.829
No.

00:07:56.247 --> 00:08:00.001
It's someone
who has too many reasons not to lose.

00:08:03.838 --> 00:08:04.797
Look.

00:08:06.674 --> 00:08:08.050
All of them.

00:08:08.134 --> 00:08:11.762
They're the reasons you have to win.

00:08:43.628 --> 00:08:44.670
So…

00:08:46.297 --> 00:08:48.924
you have to win, no matter what it takes.

00:08:51.218 --> 00:08:53.304
That's what you have to do.

00:09:05.608 --> 00:09:06.859
One!

00:09:07.943 --> 00:09:09.654
Is this a game of who talks first?

00:09:10.321 --> 00:09:12.948
I told you to share ideas.

00:09:13.032 --> 00:09:16.577
We should offer a sincere apology
and promise it won't happen again--

00:09:16.661 --> 00:09:17.495
Next.

00:09:17.578 --> 00:09:20.039
We should disclose
the construction process

00:09:20.122 --> 00:09:23.042
to restore trust
after the shoddy construction scandal--

00:09:23.125 --> 00:09:24.001
Next.

00:09:24.085 --> 00:09:28.589
We should promote our financial stability
to keep shareholders from pulling out…

00:09:31.676 --> 00:09:33.302
You know,

00:09:33.386 --> 00:09:36.180
you directors
are the people I envy the most.

00:09:36.889 --> 00:09:40.226
You get regular paychecks
even when you're so incompetent.

00:09:40.309 --> 00:09:43.354
What a great life.

00:09:46.982 --> 00:09:48.109
Listen carefully.

00:09:50.861 --> 00:09:54.323
Cut the prices
of the Oman New Town units in half.

00:09:55.366 --> 00:09:58.369
Exceptional prices, premium materials,

00:09:58.452 --> 00:10:00.955
unlimited free safety inspections.

00:10:01.038 --> 00:10:03.040
Promote them aggressively,

00:10:03.124 --> 00:10:06.210
and get Korea's top celebrities

00:10:06.293 --> 00:10:09.255
to be the faces of the campaign.

00:10:09.338 --> 00:10:10.172
But sir,

00:10:11.006 --> 00:10:13.134
our budget…

00:10:22.017 --> 00:10:23.436
Shouldn't we scrape together

00:10:23.519 --> 00:10:26.897
every last penny
to save our company, Director?

00:10:30.317 --> 00:10:31.652
What about public opinion?

00:10:31.736 --> 00:10:36.323
The hashtag "Taesan survivor"
is still spreading on social media,

00:10:37.116 --> 00:10:38.701
and the legacy media

00:10:38.784 --> 00:10:43.497
is publishing a flood
of negative stories about Taesan.

00:10:43.581 --> 00:10:45.875
Social media is one thing,

00:10:45.958 --> 00:10:49.003
but the press isn't cooperating at all.

00:10:52.923 --> 00:10:54.216
So you mean

00:10:54.300 --> 00:10:57.803
the press is the problem right now.

00:10:59.096 --> 00:11:01.432
Please have mercy, sir!

00:11:08.564 --> 00:11:11.984
The Ministry of Land, Infrastructure,
and Transport is making a fuss.

00:11:12.067 --> 00:11:13.360
They're even talking about

00:11:13.944 --> 00:11:17.031
a full-scale inspection
on True Value's shoddy construction.

00:11:17.114 --> 00:11:20.117
It was more than
just a few cracks in the wall.

00:11:20.201 --> 00:11:22.828
The higher-ups are extremely unhappy

00:11:22.912 --> 00:11:24.997
about this scandal breaking
before the election.

00:11:25.080 --> 00:11:26.290
We've got a long road ahead.

00:11:26.373 --> 00:11:28.792
We'll all end up dead
if we keep driving with a flat tire.

00:11:28.876 --> 00:11:30.169
We have to replace it.

00:11:36.592 --> 00:11:37.676
What?

00:12:00.324 --> 00:12:01.700
I've picked out

00:12:03.077 --> 00:12:04.870
your burial plots in Taegowon.

00:12:05.538 --> 00:12:08.541
I already dug
four nice little holes for you.

00:12:09.250 --> 00:12:11.877
Pick the tree you want to grow there.

00:12:12.503 --> 00:12:15.756
I thought you'd be busy,
so I brought them to you myself.

00:12:17.424 --> 00:12:20.678
Our Supreme Court Justice
values integrity,

00:12:20.761 --> 00:12:22.304
so how about a pine tree?

00:12:23.764 --> 00:12:26.934
And for our Senior Secretary,
who seems quite impatient,

00:12:27.017 --> 00:12:29.436
a plum blossom
so you'll learn perseverance.

00:12:30.145 --> 00:12:31.564
All right.

00:12:31.647 --> 00:12:34.400
Pick the tree you'd like.

00:12:34.483 --> 00:12:36.735
What on earth are you doing?

00:12:36.819 --> 00:12:38.320
Arrogant bastard.

00:12:38.404 --> 00:12:40.823
What? "Arrogant"?

00:12:41.865 --> 00:12:44.952
Are you deaf, or are you stupid?

00:12:46.120 --> 00:12:49.748
I just picked out burial plots for you.

00:12:49.832 --> 00:12:53.669
If you don't get your act together,
I'm going to bury you!

00:12:55.129 --> 00:12:57.339
The press is making quite a fuss.

00:12:58.090 --> 00:13:00.009
You should fix this, don't you think?

00:13:01.635 --> 00:13:04.430
Stop thinking about replacing the tire

00:13:04.513 --> 00:13:06.890
and find a way to keep the car rolling.

00:13:09.476 --> 00:13:10.728
If I go down…

00:13:13.063 --> 00:13:14.982
you're all going down with me.

00:13:19.778 --> 00:13:21.238
So please,

00:13:22.197 --> 00:13:24.700
keep that in mind!

00:13:24.783 --> 00:13:27.036
Remember that! All right?

00:13:30.706 --> 00:13:31.957
This is

00:13:33.042 --> 00:13:34.251
my final warning.

00:13:43.510 --> 00:13:46.180
THE LATE PARK YONG-MAN

00:13:54.897 --> 00:13:56.482
Our old boss

00:13:57.232 --> 00:13:58.984
always used to come here

00:13:59.068 --> 00:14:01.153
after a big event.

00:14:02.237 --> 00:14:04.865
Even when we said
we booked a hotel buffet,

00:14:04.948 --> 00:14:09.453
he'd say, "Putting on belly fat
will make your punches slower!"

00:14:09.536 --> 00:14:12.373
But even as he said that,

00:14:12.456 --> 00:14:16.085
he'd eat stuff like sweet and sour pork
and braised pork belly.

00:14:16.627 --> 00:14:18.629
I miss him smacking the back of my head.

00:14:19.630 --> 00:14:21.757
Whenever I was working alone at night,

00:14:21.840 --> 00:14:26.387
he'd say, "Hey, Je-gil, why are you
always working on that laptop?"

00:14:26.470 --> 00:14:30.224
"You'll ruin your eyes.
Keep the lights on when you're working."

00:14:30.307 --> 00:14:33.811
He used to tell me
I had to keep my belly full to punch well

00:14:34.770 --> 00:14:36.855
and that it's miserable
living on an empty stomach.

00:14:37.815 --> 00:14:39.984
I'm so full right now,

00:14:40.943 --> 00:14:43.362
but I don't know why I feel so miserable.

00:14:58.460 --> 00:15:03.257
CONGRATULATIONS ON YOUR RETIREMENT

00:15:08.470 --> 00:15:10.681
Isn't this cape a bit much?

00:15:10.764 --> 00:15:12.474
-It looks good.
-It looks good.

00:15:13.809 --> 00:15:16.145
We already booked the hotel
and everything,

00:15:16.228 --> 00:15:17.688
but you just had to come here.

00:15:17.771 --> 00:15:19.023
Don't be silly.

00:15:19.690 --> 00:15:22.401
Since when did we start getting fancy
and going to hotels?

00:15:22.484 --> 00:15:23.736
A retirement ceremony

00:15:24.528 --> 00:15:27.239
should be done at a place like this,
with black bean noodles.

00:15:27.322 --> 00:15:29.908
Who holds a retirement ceremony
at a Chinese restaurant?

00:15:29.992 --> 00:15:31.452
Shut it.

00:15:32.327 --> 00:15:33.495
I started this job

00:15:33.579 --> 00:15:36.165
so I could eat
as much black bean noodles as I wanted.

00:15:36.248 --> 00:15:37.666
CHEERS TO YONG-MAN'S NEW BEGINNING!

00:15:37.750 --> 00:15:40.085
And I actually did eat them
to my heart's content

00:15:40.169 --> 00:15:42.171
working in this field all these years.

00:15:43.047 --> 00:15:44.673
Now that I'm retired,

00:15:45.841 --> 00:15:48.761
I won't eat any black bean noodles again
until I'm dead.

00:15:48.844 --> 00:15:50.888
So congratulate me now.

00:15:51.472 --> 00:15:53.515
I am free.

00:15:54.391 --> 00:15:56.268
-Congratulations!
-Congratulations!

00:16:01.523 --> 00:16:04.735
Congratulations on your retirement

00:16:04.818 --> 00:16:07.613
Congratulations on your retirement

00:16:07.696 --> 00:16:10.908
Congratulations, dear Boss

00:16:10.991 --> 00:16:14.078
Congratulations on your retirement

00:16:15.662 --> 00:16:17.581
-Congratulations!
-You punk.

00:16:19.291 --> 00:16:20.292
Thank you.

00:16:22.920 --> 00:16:26.340
Now that you're retired,
can't you just live with me…

00:16:29.551 --> 00:16:32.387
and be my father?

00:16:40.062 --> 00:16:41.897
You're pretty drunk.

00:16:43.482 --> 00:16:44.817
I mean it.

00:16:46.443 --> 00:16:47.861
Park Hae-kang.

00:16:48.445 --> 00:16:52.533
I didn't invest in you
to be treated like your father.

00:16:53.283 --> 00:16:56.370
You don't have to repay me.

00:16:58.497 --> 00:17:00.916
I'm not saying that
because I feel indebted.

00:17:02.126 --> 00:17:04.128
I just want to call you my father.

00:17:07.506 --> 00:17:10.300
Don't call me your father.
It makes me cringe.

00:17:11.844 --> 00:17:15.514
Let's not make things harder
for each other by acting like a family.

00:17:15.597 --> 00:17:16.682
Got that?

00:17:18.016 --> 00:17:19.476
That's not fair.

00:17:20.144 --> 00:17:22.146
You did everything for me,

00:17:22.229 --> 00:17:24.982
yet you won't even let me
call you my father.

00:17:25.065 --> 00:17:27.484
Fine, I won't do it.

00:17:27.568 --> 00:17:30.279
"Father"? Forget it.

00:17:33.574 --> 00:17:36.535
I love you, son.

00:17:42.749 --> 00:17:45.419
THE LATE PARK YONG-MAN

00:17:51.675 --> 00:17:56.555
You're the type to save people
even if you planned to do something bad.

00:17:56.638 --> 00:17:58.140
I know you.

00:18:08.192 --> 00:18:09.193
You had no idea.

00:18:10.569 --> 00:18:12.321
I deceived you.

00:18:13.447 --> 00:18:14.448
But…

00:18:15.449 --> 00:18:17.159
I'll live my life

00:18:18.118 --> 00:18:20.037
proving that you were right.

00:18:25.959 --> 00:18:27.586
What should I do about this?

00:18:27.669 --> 00:18:30.881
I kept it as leverage,
as you told me to yesterday.

00:18:30.964 --> 00:18:33.467
We've learned that stuff like this
won't be enough.

00:18:34.968 --> 00:18:37.387
Get rid of it. Park Yong-man is dead too.

00:18:39.598 --> 00:18:41.225
But one thing I'm worried about

00:18:41.308 --> 00:18:43.560
is that Park Hae-kang
has nothing to lose now,

00:18:43.644 --> 00:18:46.188
so we don't know what he might do.

00:18:46.772 --> 00:18:49.816
And if he finds out that
we covered up the Park Yong-man case…

00:18:50.400 --> 00:18:51.443
Exactly.

00:18:52.569 --> 00:18:55.906
Park Hae-kang and Lee Chung-won
are both crazy.

00:18:55.989 --> 00:18:59.701
So shouldn't we hide behind
the more powerful one in this situation?

00:18:59.785 --> 00:19:02.037
TAESAN CONSTRUCTION LEE CHUNG-WON

00:19:02.871 --> 00:19:05.624
Yes, Mr. Lee. I was going to call you.

00:19:07.960 --> 00:19:08.919
Pardon?

00:19:10.337 --> 00:19:11.755
Congratulations.

00:19:13.006 --> 00:19:16.510
You've just become
a member of our One Club.

00:19:17.094 --> 00:19:20.847
It's a reward for covering up
what happened with Park Yong-man.

00:19:20.931 --> 00:19:21.932
Thank you.

00:19:22.933 --> 00:19:26.311
We're truly on the same side now.

00:19:26.395 --> 00:19:27.229
Yes, sir.

00:19:27.896 --> 00:19:29.898
I'll see you at the welcome ceremony.

00:19:32.734 --> 00:19:34.361
We found Choi Yeong-jae, sir.

00:19:35.320 --> 00:19:36.321
Really?

00:19:36.947 --> 00:19:38.532
Where was he hiding?

00:19:38.615 --> 00:19:41.493
We got the security footage
around his house,

00:19:41.576 --> 00:19:44.538
and it seems like he was struggling
with the tenants' council president

00:19:44.621 --> 00:19:46.164
and got caught by Park Hae-kang's men.

00:19:46.248 --> 00:19:48.125
He's in the closed kindergarten now.

00:19:48.709 --> 00:19:50.294
We'll get him immediately.

00:19:51.586 --> 00:19:52.879
All right.

00:19:53.755 --> 00:19:56.675
What tree would suit him?

00:19:57.342 --> 00:19:58.552
Also,

00:19:58.635 --> 00:20:01.763
things seem to be getting worse
among the True Value residents.

00:20:01.847 --> 00:20:03.056
Park Hae-kang aside,

00:20:03.140 --> 00:20:07.269
the tenants' council president
keeps stirring up public opinion.

00:20:08.228 --> 00:20:11.315
That pageant woman again?

00:20:12.441 --> 00:20:14.985
Should we try giving her some money?

00:20:16.278 --> 00:20:18.697
Mr. Kim.

00:20:20.198 --> 00:20:22.117
People like that are more obsessed

00:20:22.200 --> 00:20:26.204
with climbing the social ladder
than money.

00:20:28.540 --> 00:20:31.335
You've been losing your touch these days.

00:20:33.045 --> 00:20:34.212
I'll make the preparations.

00:20:38.633 --> 00:20:41.636
TENANTS' COUNCIL
PRESIDENT JANG SUK-JIN

00:20:43.013 --> 00:20:44.348
OMAN NEW TOWN RESIDENTS' FORUM

00:20:44.431 --> 00:20:47.392
TAESAN'S "HALF-PRICE BARGAIN"?
HOW CAN YOU SLEEP ON A PILE OF TRASH?

00:20:47.976 --> 00:20:49.186
Who is it?

00:20:55.525 --> 00:20:56.360
Wow.

00:20:56.860 --> 00:21:01.490
This place is completely different
from when President Seo was here.

00:21:02.157 --> 00:21:03.658
I'm Lee Chung-won.

00:21:07.162 --> 00:21:08.830
I'm well aware.

00:21:08.914 --> 00:21:10.457
I've been posting your face

00:21:10.540 --> 00:21:14.169
on our online forum dozens of times a day.

00:21:14.252 --> 00:21:16.546
Of course I know you.

00:21:16.630 --> 00:21:18.465
So what brings you here?

00:21:21.718 --> 00:21:23.887
A penthouse in Oman New Town.

00:21:24.554 --> 00:21:27.808
I've set one aside just for you.

00:21:35.107 --> 00:21:35.982
TRUE VALUE STATE OMAN

00:21:36.983 --> 00:21:38.026
265-SQUARE-METER PENTHOUSE

00:21:38.610 --> 00:21:39.569
It's 265 square meters?

00:21:42.197 --> 00:21:44.991
Oh my. The view is amazing.

00:21:45.075 --> 00:21:49.246
It's on a whole different level
compared to our True Value.

00:21:49.830 --> 00:21:52.499
Why don't you stop
all this exhausting work now?

00:21:52.582 --> 00:21:57.462
All you have to do is say that
Taesan is providing proper compensation

00:21:58.130 --> 00:22:00.132
to the residents.

00:22:04.136 --> 00:22:05.971
But too bad.

00:22:06.721 --> 00:22:11.643
I want something
much more expensive than this.

00:22:13.019 --> 00:22:14.104
More expensive?

00:22:21.987 --> 00:22:25.907
The long-term repair reserve fund
that you embezzled

00:22:26.658 --> 00:22:30.036
and the money you siphoned off
by stuffing trash in our walls

00:22:30.120 --> 00:22:32.080
instead of proper materials.

00:22:32.164 --> 00:22:33.957
With all that combined…

00:22:36.001 --> 00:22:38.962
not even ten penthouses like this
would be enough.

00:22:39.546 --> 00:22:40.547
Don't you think?

00:22:41.506 --> 00:22:45.302
I graduated top of my class
from Ilhwa Women's University.

00:22:45.969 --> 00:22:50.640
I can tell the difference
between what's crap and what's good.

00:22:51.850 --> 00:22:52.851
What?

00:22:55.645 --> 00:22:56.688
I'm saying

00:22:58.023 --> 00:22:59.649
you're crap.

00:23:00.609 --> 00:23:01.902
So get lost, you thief.

00:23:04.279 --> 00:23:06.198
Don't you dare try such cheap tricks.

00:23:06.698 --> 00:23:08.116
Throw salt on him!

00:23:21.046 --> 00:23:22.047
You're beautiful.

00:23:26.009 --> 00:23:27.093
Gross.

00:23:33.225 --> 00:23:35.560
Park Hae-kang really is a mystery.

00:23:37.604 --> 00:23:40.273
How is everyone around him

00:23:41.066 --> 00:23:42.150
equally crazy?

00:23:50.200 --> 00:23:51.243
UNBEATABLE PRICES

00:23:51.326 --> 00:23:53.286
TAESAN CONSTRUCTION WILL BE REBORN

00:23:53.370 --> 00:23:54.829
SHOCKING PRICES FROM 10 YEARS AGO!

00:23:56.915 --> 00:23:58.750
Gyeong-nam, stop the car.

00:23:59.793 --> 00:24:00.794
Yes, Boss.

00:24:07.050 --> 00:24:08.260
"Reborn"?

00:24:08.843 --> 00:24:10.637
He's never even died before.

00:24:10.720 --> 00:24:12.973
Does that jerk really think
this will work?

00:24:13.056 --> 00:24:15.892
Everyone in Korea just saw trash
pouring out of the walls.

00:24:16.476 --> 00:24:19.020
Well, money makes people blind.

00:24:19.604 --> 00:24:22.107
And Lee Chung-won
is well aware of that fact.

00:24:25.360 --> 00:24:27.195
TAESAN CONSTRUCTION CONTROVERSY

00:24:27.279 --> 00:24:31.574
PUBLIC APOLOGY AND NEXT COURSE OF ACTION

00:24:48.008 --> 00:24:49.968
My fellow citizens, I am deeply sorry.

00:24:51.970 --> 00:24:55.557
We betrayed the valuable trust you had

00:24:55.640 --> 00:24:57.684
in our brand, Taesan.

00:24:58.268 --> 00:25:01.855
As part of our efforts
to take responsibility for this incident,

00:25:02.439 --> 00:25:04.441
Taesan Construction will supply

00:25:05.942 --> 00:25:09.237
affordable housing
through a social contribution program

00:25:09.321 --> 00:25:12.824
and restore the trust you've given us.

00:25:12.907 --> 00:25:15.201
A key part of the administration's
housing supply policy,

00:25:15.285 --> 00:25:17.412
the first housing application
in the fourth new town

00:25:17.495 --> 00:25:20.457
recorded an average
competition rate of 98 to 1.

00:25:20.540 --> 00:25:24.419
Oman New Town drew strong interest
with its affordable prices

00:25:24.502 --> 00:25:26.087
and excellent location.

00:25:26.171 --> 00:25:29.007
Among them, Taesan Construction's
public housing supply

00:25:29.090 --> 00:25:30.425
for social contribution

00:25:30.508 --> 00:25:34.054
recorded an even higher competition rate
of 957 to 1.

00:25:34.137 --> 00:25:36.598
We will use this as an opportunity
to make major changes

00:25:36.681 --> 00:25:39.476
and ensure that such an incident
never happens again.

00:25:39.559 --> 00:25:41.436
We will make fundamental changes

00:25:42.103 --> 00:25:43.438
and be reborn.

00:25:54.074 --> 00:25:56.201
Despite the controversy
over shoddy construction,

00:25:56.284 --> 00:26:00.372
Taesan's housing program recorded
the highest-ever application rate,

00:26:00.455 --> 00:26:04.000
and Taesan Construction's stock
closed at the daily limit today.

00:26:04.084 --> 00:26:05.001
Reporter Kim Jin-su…

00:26:05.085 --> 00:26:06.336
HIGH COMPETITION FOR OMAN NEW TOWN

00:26:06.419 --> 00:26:08.004
They were all barking,

00:26:08.088 --> 00:26:12.300
but they wag their tails
the moment I throw them a bone.

00:26:14.302 --> 00:26:15.762
Geez.

00:26:16.971 --> 00:26:18.515
TRUE VALUE STATE OMAN

00:26:22.560 --> 00:26:25.772
People are saying getting a Taesan
apartment is like winning the lottery.

00:26:26.439 --> 00:26:29.943
How can they react like that
when they know what Taesan did?

00:26:30.026 --> 00:26:32.445
The greed for winning the lottery

00:26:32.529 --> 00:26:35.532
is stronger than their fear
of shoddy construction.

00:26:35.615 --> 00:26:37.367
What do we do now?

00:26:37.450 --> 00:26:38.326
Mr. Kim.

00:26:40.620 --> 00:26:41.913
This won't do.

00:26:41.996 --> 00:26:44.791
Whether it's Taesan or Chung-won,
we'll just wipe them out.

00:26:45.542 --> 00:26:48.586
We're retired,
but let's go with our old methods.

00:26:49.254 --> 00:26:51.089
A bloody revenge for our old boss…

00:26:51.172 --> 00:26:52.340
I'm in.

00:26:52.424 --> 00:26:53.508
What's with you?

00:26:54.259 --> 00:26:56.261
I'll get my weapons.

00:27:05.562 --> 00:27:06.479
Boss.

00:27:06.563 --> 00:27:08.565
I'm ready to risk my life for this.

00:27:08.648 --> 00:27:09.816
Just give the word.

00:27:09.899 --> 00:27:11.234
And I'm saying this just in case,

00:27:11.317 --> 00:27:13.903
but don't tell us that you'll go
and fight by yourself.

00:27:14.737 --> 00:27:15.947
This time, we won't listen--

00:27:16.030 --> 00:27:17.282
Why would I?

00:27:20.118 --> 00:27:23.246
I have a family. Why would I fight alone?

00:27:24.414 --> 00:27:25.582
Family?

00:27:28.626 --> 00:27:29.752
Get up.

00:27:33.339 --> 00:27:35.049
Guys. Lizard.

00:27:35.133 --> 00:27:36.718
Ms. Kang Ha-ri, Kang Ha-jeong.

00:27:37.594 --> 00:27:39.012
Please help me

00:27:39.888 --> 00:27:41.514
so I can win this fight.

00:27:42.432 --> 00:27:43.683
I need your help.

00:27:44.726 --> 00:27:46.895
-He's changed.
-Boss.

00:27:48.354 --> 00:27:49.939
I'm a bit old,

00:27:50.023 --> 00:27:52.358
but I'll help in any way I can.

00:27:52.442 --> 00:27:53.985
I won't ask for money this time.

00:27:54.068 --> 00:27:55.570
I'll give you a family discount.

00:27:55.653 --> 00:27:57.697
I'll do anything I can to help too.

00:27:58.740 --> 00:28:00.033
What should we do first, Boss?

00:28:01.159 --> 00:28:03.411
We should start
by taking what's precious to him.

00:28:03.995 --> 00:28:06.789
Public opinion and the law
aren't enough to defeat him.

00:28:06.873 --> 00:28:09.584
We'll have to use our own method.

00:28:13.379 --> 00:28:15.089
So what is it?

00:28:38.863 --> 00:28:41.282
See? I told you they'd come.

00:28:43.576 --> 00:28:47.997
Mr. Choi, if you don't listen to us,
you'll really be sent to the afterlife.

00:28:48.081 --> 00:28:50.041
-Je-gil, go.
-Okay.

00:29:00.301 --> 00:29:01.928
Stop dragging that!

00:29:06.057 --> 00:29:07.058
What about me?

00:29:12.146 --> 00:29:13.857
Was this really our best option?

00:29:15.108 --> 00:29:18.111
We have another mouth to feed now.
Our living expenses…

00:29:23.908 --> 00:29:25.326
How long have you been the manager?

00:29:26.619 --> 00:29:28.329
Do you want to lose this hand?

00:29:28.413 --> 00:29:31.207
All my joints are aching

00:29:31.291 --> 00:29:34.002
from staying trapped in the kindergarten.

00:29:34.085 --> 00:29:37.130
How did you know
this stuff is good for your joints?

00:29:37.714 --> 00:29:40.300
This is supposed to be good
for sore knees, right?

00:29:40.383 --> 00:29:42.176
It's good for stiff shoulders too.

00:29:42.260 --> 00:29:45.013
I had six pills for each meal,
and it was really effective.

00:29:45.096 --> 00:29:47.265
Geez. No wonder
they disappeared so quickly.

00:29:47.348 --> 00:29:50.476
Don't you know what they say
about overusing medicine?

00:29:50.560 --> 00:29:52.145
The recommended amount is two pills!

00:29:52.228 --> 00:29:54.439
He doesn't know what that means.

00:29:55.189 --> 00:29:57.734
Mr. Choi, have it with water.

00:29:58.318 --> 00:29:59.861
Thanks, Ha-jeong.

00:29:59.944 --> 00:30:02.071
Are you seriously accepting that?

00:30:02.155 --> 00:30:05.575
Did you forget how you framed
my sister and Mr. Park for embezzlement?

00:30:05.658 --> 00:30:07.410
You little…

00:30:07.493 --> 00:30:08.536
Well…

00:30:09.370 --> 00:30:11.372
I only did as Mr. Lee ordered.

00:30:11.456 --> 00:30:14.000
Taegowon isn't just a tree farm, is it?

00:30:14.083 --> 00:30:15.084
Where's the money?

00:30:15.168 --> 00:30:17.420
I don't know that either.

00:30:17.503 --> 00:30:18.588
But…

00:30:19.422 --> 00:30:21.424
whenever we took money out of the fund,

00:30:21.507 --> 00:30:23.885
we delivered it to Taegowon.

00:30:23.968 --> 00:30:25.386
Me and President Seo.

00:30:25.970 --> 00:30:28.806
In any case, all the money
embezzled from apartment complexes

00:30:28.890 --> 00:30:30.600
must all be there somewhere.

00:30:32.143 --> 00:30:34.771
Then our 17.8 billion should be there too.

00:30:34.854 --> 00:30:36.481
That 17.8 billion.

00:30:37.106 --> 00:30:38.107
Should we steal it back?

00:30:38.191 --> 00:30:39.859
-Of course.
-Sounds good.

00:30:40.568 --> 00:30:43.821
Yes. Lee Chung-won
values that more than his life.

00:30:43.905 --> 00:30:45.782
Let's take these

00:30:45.865 --> 00:30:48.368
and strip him bare.

00:30:48.451 --> 00:30:49.452
Yes, Boss.

00:30:50.286 --> 00:30:51.371
All right.

00:31:06.803 --> 00:31:08.930
You lost Choi Yeong-jae again?

00:31:09.806 --> 00:31:10.848
Mr. Kim.

00:31:11.557 --> 00:31:12.392
No…

00:31:17.522 --> 00:31:18.523
Eun-ho.

00:31:19.190 --> 00:31:21.776
You weren't like this before.

00:31:22.902 --> 00:31:24.320
I'm sorry, sir.

00:31:25.363 --> 00:31:28.741
When we were swinging steel pipes
at demolition sites,

00:31:29.701 --> 00:31:33.371
you were full of ruthless determination.

00:31:34.038 --> 00:31:35.248
We came

00:31:36.374 --> 00:31:38.584
all the way here with that determination.

00:31:40.503 --> 00:31:41.629
I'm sorry, sir.

00:31:42.588 --> 00:31:45.466
There's no point
in looking decent on the outside…

00:31:48.302 --> 00:31:49.262
if this…

00:31:51.806 --> 00:31:52.849
this…

00:31:55.852 --> 00:31:56.936
and this…

00:31:58.396 --> 00:32:00.523
have all lost that determination.

00:32:11.701 --> 00:32:14.495
Park Hae-kang
even took Choi Yeong-jae now.

00:32:15.705 --> 00:32:18.124
I'm so jealous.

00:32:20.251 --> 00:32:22.295
What will his next step be?

00:32:23.588 --> 00:32:24.797
I'm so curious.

00:32:47.361 --> 00:32:50.281
Look at this.
It's practically a fortress, not a farm.

00:32:50.364 --> 00:32:52.575
They've got infrared sensors
set up everywhere,

00:32:52.658 --> 00:32:56.287
and their guards aren't hired muscle.
They're security consulting professionals.

00:32:56.370 --> 00:32:58.247
So we can't face them head-on.

00:32:58.331 --> 00:33:00.249
And it's not like
we can fly in like drones.

00:33:00.333 --> 00:33:01.709
Do we have to dig through?

00:33:01.793 --> 00:33:03.753
-Then I'll go get shovels.
-Hey.

00:33:03.836 --> 00:33:06.047
He was just saying that.
Do you take him for a fool?

00:33:08.299 --> 00:33:09.717
If we can't go inside…

00:33:12.762 --> 00:33:14.388
we can make them come out.

00:33:15.932 --> 00:33:17.475
Is this the district office?

00:33:17.558 --> 00:33:19.894
I'd like to report
illegally dumped waste from Taegowon.

00:33:19.977 --> 00:33:21.020
Illegal dumping!

00:33:21.104 --> 00:33:24.023
Hello, I'm a reporter
from Gongyeong Daily.

00:33:24.107 --> 00:33:25.858
Are there any plans
to investigate Taegowon?

00:33:26.526 --> 00:33:29.779
There's a stench of rotten meat
coming from Taegowon.

00:33:29.862 --> 00:33:31.864
I'm sure there's some
illegal butchering going on.

00:33:31.948 --> 00:33:34.659
Shouldn't you be doing
an emergency health inspection?

00:33:38.663 --> 00:33:39.789
Is this the district office?

00:33:39.872 --> 00:33:42.500
Yes, I'm hearing screaming every night
coming from Taegowon.

00:33:42.583 --> 00:33:44.919
They must be burying people in there.

00:33:46.879 --> 00:33:48.673
I'm a former guard from there.

00:33:48.756 --> 00:33:51.384
They have a dog farm in their basement.

00:33:51.467 --> 00:33:53.636
They even hunt and eat protected animals.

00:33:53.719 --> 00:33:55.138
If you don't believe me, go and…

00:33:55.221 --> 00:33:56.722
Is this the inspection office?

00:33:56.806 --> 00:34:01.435
I'd like to report the Environmental
Department for neglecting their duties…

00:34:02.270 --> 00:34:03.938
If you don't crack down on them now,

00:34:04.021 --> 00:34:06.399
we'll consider it collusion
and report it to the press.

00:34:09.610 --> 00:34:10.444
ENVIRONMENTAL DEPARTMENT

00:34:10.528 --> 00:34:13.573
Leachate? That's a tree farm, though.

00:34:13.656 --> 00:34:16.033
A party with drugs?
Then you should call the police…

00:34:16.617 --> 00:34:19.078
What? Dereliction of duty?

00:34:19.162 --> 00:34:20.246
An audit?

00:34:20.329 --> 00:34:21.956
Why would you audit our… Hello?

00:34:22.039 --> 00:34:25.334
Hey! What the hell
is this fuss about Taegowon?

00:34:25.418 --> 00:34:27.378
We're getting reports on illegal dumping,

00:34:27.461 --> 00:34:29.672
illegal drug use,
and that it's a drug den.

00:34:29.755 --> 00:34:31.841
Even environmental groups
received the reports.

00:34:31.924 --> 00:34:34.927
If we don't send someone,
the website will crash from complaints.

00:34:35.011 --> 00:34:38.139
Hey, gather a team
and go check Taegowon immediately!

00:34:46.647 --> 00:34:49.984
Mr. Lee, do we have to trim these today?

00:34:50.693 --> 00:34:51.736
The thing about trees

00:34:51.819 --> 00:34:55.281
is that they have to be frightened
for them to take a beautiful shape.

00:34:55.364 --> 00:34:59.660
So it's the perfect time to shape them,
just like you.

00:34:59.744 --> 00:35:01.954
Was threatening us
at the hotel not enough?

00:35:03.873 --> 00:35:07.210
I'm just saying
you won't have to get your hands dirty.

00:35:07.293 --> 00:35:11.881
I just got a useful tool
that can take care of all the hard work.

00:35:19.764 --> 00:35:21.807
It's nice to see you, sirs.

00:35:26.103 --> 00:35:27.104
I'm Kwak Ju-gwon.

00:35:27.188 --> 00:35:31.817
Together with all of you,
I'll properly prune this country.

00:35:33.110 --> 00:35:35.238
Did you get the ten billion?

00:35:35.321 --> 00:35:38.324
Or did you two make
some kind of deal behind our backs?

00:35:38.908 --> 00:35:42.870
Taesan has been in hot water lately
because of the shoddy construction.

00:35:42.954 --> 00:35:45.790
You're going to have to become
our shield, Commissioner.

00:35:46.499 --> 00:35:47.667
Don't worry.

00:35:47.750 --> 00:35:50.461
My specialty is paving the road ahead

00:35:50.544 --> 00:35:53.256
so you won't have to deal
with any dust flying around.

00:35:53.756 --> 00:35:54.882
You heard that, right?

00:35:54.966 --> 00:35:58.427
Our new member is great
at taking care of the cleanup.

00:35:58.511 --> 00:36:00.763
So don't worry about a flat tire.

00:36:00.846 --> 00:36:05.017
Commissioner Kwak is going to have
the entire road blocked off.

00:36:05.601 --> 00:36:06.602
Round of applause.

00:36:11.732 --> 00:36:13.192
OFFICIAL DUTY

00:36:15.820 --> 00:36:17.446
Hello.

00:36:17.530 --> 00:36:18.656
What is this about?

00:36:18.739 --> 00:36:20.866
-We're from the district office.
-The district office?

00:36:20.950 --> 00:36:22.285
They came by this morning.

00:36:22.368 --> 00:36:24.036
We're from the department above them.

00:36:24.120 --> 00:36:25.162
The department above them?

00:36:25.246 --> 00:36:26.872
This is a serious matter.

00:36:26.956 --> 00:36:28.791
With everything going on,

00:36:28.874 --> 00:36:31.544
we have no choice
but to conduct a thorough investigation.

00:36:31.627 --> 00:36:33.421
What more are you trying to investigate?

00:36:33.504 --> 00:36:35.506
What on earth are you doing in here?

00:36:35.589 --> 00:36:36.465
What are you doing?

00:36:36.549 --> 00:36:37.925
This isn't a tree farm, is it?

00:36:38.009 --> 00:36:39.260
-We already know.
-Calm down.

00:36:39.343 --> 00:36:40.344
We're getting complaints!

00:36:40.428 --> 00:36:41.804
The higher-ups are throwing a fit!

00:36:41.887 --> 00:36:43.723
-I wish I could tell you--
-Enough!

00:36:44.849 --> 00:36:46.767
We came here first
because it'll get out of hand

00:36:46.851 --> 00:36:47.977
if the police come too.

00:36:48.060 --> 00:36:49.729
So please understand.

00:36:49.812 --> 00:36:51.647
There are guests present.

00:36:51.731 --> 00:36:53.232
Please return tomorrow morning.

00:36:53.316 --> 00:36:55.067
This makes it seem more suspicious.

00:36:55.151 --> 00:36:56.819
Mr. Jang, call the cops.

00:36:56.902 --> 00:36:58.321
We'll come back with the police.

00:36:58.404 --> 00:37:00.364
Why are they complicating things?

00:37:00.448 --> 00:37:01.699
Wait!

00:37:02.575 --> 00:37:04.201
It's fine. We'll come with the police.

00:37:04.285 --> 00:37:05.161
Right.

00:37:05.244 --> 00:37:06.120
Wait…

00:37:07.621 --> 00:37:09.373
Please make it fast.

00:37:09.457 --> 00:37:10.708
-Shall we?
-Sure.

00:37:10.791 --> 00:37:11.792
-Shall we?
-Make it quick?

00:37:11.876 --> 00:37:13.336
-Then check thoroughly.
-Okay.

00:37:13.419 --> 00:37:16.130
We have to report this to our chief,
so take photos too. Let's go.

00:37:16.714 --> 00:37:18.758
We're not some random weirdos.

00:37:18.841 --> 00:37:21.844
You shouldn't interfere
with government duties.

00:37:24.597 --> 00:37:25.890
-Don't look back.
-What is it?

00:37:25.973 --> 00:37:26.849
They're following us.

00:37:26.932 --> 00:37:28.392
Keep looking forward. Act natural.

00:37:35.649 --> 00:37:36.692
You're all gathered here.

00:37:37.526 --> 00:37:39.487
What kind of performance is this?

00:37:39.570 --> 00:37:41.572
-Only authorized personnel…
-Sure.

00:37:41.655 --> 00:37:44.075
Supreme Court Justice,
Senior Secretary for Civil Affairs,

00:37:45.076 --> 00:37:47.495
Prosecutor General,
President of Gongyeong Daily,

00:37:48.120 --> 00:37:49.246
and…

00:37:50.081 --> 00:37:52.333
our new member, Commissioner Kwak.

00:37:52.416 --> 00:37:55.127
After all that fuss, you finally got in.

00:37:56.796 --> 00:37:58.464
The One Club sure is something.

00:37:59.465 --> 00:38:02.051
You're Korea's most powerful figures,

00:38:02.134 --> 00:38:05.763
and you're just sitting here
trimming trees?

00:38:05.846 --> 00:38:08.057
Mr. Lee, what are you doing? Kick him out.

00:38:08.641 --> 00:38:09.725
Park Hae-kang.

00:38:10.810 --> 00:38:13.312
Do you have a death wish?

00:38:13.396 --> 00:38:16.399
Taegowon. Tae, meaning big.
Go, meaning high.

00:38:16.482 --> 00:38:19.193
For a place with such a lofty name,

00:38:19.276 --> 00:38:21.779
what lies beneath is pretty rotten.

00:38:21.862 --> 00:38:24.156
How dare you speak that way
in front of us?

00:38:25.241 --> 00:38:27.493
I have something to show you.

00:38:27.576 --> 00:38:29.537
I took some photos on the way,

00:38:29.620 --> 00:38:32.373
and they have such pretty nameplates
for every tree.

00:38:32.456 --> 00:38:34.291
They're called memorial trees.

00:38:34.375 --> 00:38:37.294
This one's name is Kim Hong-hyeon.

00:38:37.378 --> 00:38:38.712
Taesan's finance team leader

00:38:38.796 --> 00:38:41.006
who supposedly fled overseas
five years ago.

00:38:41.841 --> 00:38:43.676
And this tree's name is Lee Jae-gu.

00:38:43.759 --> 00:38:47.388
Assemblyman Lee Jae-gu,
who went missing three years ago.

00:38:48.347 --> 00:38:49.932
And this one is

00:38:50.015 --> 00:38:51.559
Nam Hui-jae.

00:38:51.642 --> 00:38:54.145
Oh, right.
That's the newspaper company president.

00:38:54.687 --> 00:38:55.938
Shut up.

00:38:59.817 --> 00:39:01.152
And there was also a tree

00:39:01.235 --> 00:39:03.696
with the name of our former
residents' association president.

00:39:06.740 --> 00:39:07.825
Should I try digging?

00:39:12.246 --> 00:39:14.039
Or should I leave them be?

00:39:14.957 --> 00:39:17.918
Shut up, you bastard.

00:39:21.630 --> 00:39:23.007
You'd better hurry.

00:39:23.799 --> 00:39:26.469
Things that stink
should be cleaned quickly.

00:39:26.552 --> 00:39:27.386
Wouldn't you agree?

00:39:28.929 --> 00:39:31.098
I'll get going, then.

00:39:32.808 --> 00:39:33.809
Have a good day.

00:39:54.205 --> 00:39:57.458
Sir, it seems like
the elders have noticed.

00:39:57.541 --> 00:39:58.709
Don't worry.

00:39:58.792 --> 00:40:01.420
Those geezers
won't be able to say anything.

00:40:03.756 --> 00:40:05.883
Park Hae-kang was throwing bait.

00:40:07.051 --> 00:40:09.303
He'll be waiting for us to dig them up.

00:40:10.304 --> 00:40:12.223
Then what should we do, sir?

00:40:14.099 --> 00:40:17.311
We'll dig…

00:40:19.647 --> 00:40:21.065
just as he wants.

00:40:22.107 --> 00:40:23.150
We'll begin right away.

00:40:23.234 --> 00:40:25.027
Use rented trucks,

00:40:25.110 --> 00:40:27.488
and change all the license plates.

00:40:27.571 --> 00:40:30.741
Move everything,
and don't leave a speck of dirt behind.

00:40:31.408 --> 00:40:34.411
But Taesan's warehouse will be too risky.

00:40:38.582 --> 00:40:39.667
I know a place.

00:40:40.834 --> 00:40:42.586
Somewhere no one can even imagine.

00:41:03.774 --> 00:41:05.985
It's cramped. Stop pushing.

00:41:06.068 --> 00:41:09.321
We don't know when it'll be over,
so have at least two sandwiches.

00:41:09.405 --> 00:41:10.906
You're on your fourth one.

00:41:11.865 --> 00:41:13.117
Well, it's so good.

00:41:13.200 --> 00:41:14.410
You're right about that.

00:41:16.203 --> 00:41:17.413
They're coming out.

00:41:18.414 --> 00:41:19.665
They're coming out.

00:41:19.748 --> 00:41:21.917
Stay on your targets, everyone.

00:41:28.465 --> 00:41:30.050
That's going in the opposite direction.

00:41:30.134 --> 00:41:31.802
We're going that way.

00:41:42.605 --> 00:41:44.732
Team 1, turning left.

00:41:46.066 --> 00:41:48.110
My heart's about to burst.

00:41:48.193 --> 00:41:50.279
It's way more nerve-racking
than in the movies.

00:41:53.240 --> 00:41:56.285
Whatever's in that truck
is what we're after, right?

00:41:56.368 --> 00:42:00.497
Yes. President Park made the call,
so we should trust him.

00:42:00.581 --> 00:42:03.292
I think we just got caught
by a speed camera.

00:42:03.375 --> 00:42:05.919
My makeup's all cakey, though.
Should I touch up my lipstick?

00:42:08.380 --> 00:42:10.341
Team 2, turning right.

00:42:10.424 --> 00:42:12.009
Hold on tight.

00:42:12.092 --> 00:42:14.762
Step on it.
Let's crush them for good today.

00:42:19.016 --> 00:42:21.018
This must be the real deal.

00:42:21.101 --> 00:42:22.936
They must've noticed. They're speeding up.

00:42:23.020 --> 00:42:25.064
Mr. Kim seems to be pretty anxious.

00:42:28.317 --> 00:42:29.610
Stick closer to him.

00:43:04.353 --> 00:43:05.312
He's gone.

00:43:06.146 --> 00:43:07.981
-He left.
-Let's go.

00:43:19.702 --> 00:43:20.786
He's not coming out.

00:43:21.370 --> 00:43:23.706
He's just leaving the truck out here?

00:43:24.915 --> 00:43:25.958
Let's go.

00:43:26.041 --> 00:43:27.501
This is too easy.

00:43:28.836 --> 00:43:30.921
-Big Guy, keep an eye out.
-Okay.

00:43:36.802 --> 00:43:38.053
Open it.

00:43:41.306 --> 00:43:42.433
Oops.

00:43:43.851 --> 00:43:45.352
-What is this?
-Boss!

00:43:45.436 --> 00:43:46.270
What's going on?

00:43:53.527 --> 00:43:54.903
What's going on?

00:43:56.029 --> 00:43:57.114
It's a trap!

00:43:59.867 --> 00:44:01.744
-Are you ready?
-For what?

00:44:01.827 --> 00:44:02.786
Run!

00:44:19.136 --> 00:44:21.138
-Let's lead them to the rooftop!
-Yes, Boss!

00:44:39.281 --> 00:44:40.574
Hang in there. Don't let go.

00:44:47.122 --> 00:44:48.457
Now! Run!

00:45:56.191 --> 00:45:57.859
-Is your stomach okay?
-No, it hurts.

00:46:03.031 --> 00:46:04.199
Mr. Park! Get in!

00:46:05.200 --> 00:46:06.451
Lizard!

00:46:09.496 --> 00:46:11.331
-Park Hae-kang!
-No!

00:46:20.549 --> 00:46:21.633
Lizard.

00:46:27.097 --> 00:46:27.973
Lizard.

00:46:30.517 --> 00:46:32.436
-He got stabbed.
-Where?

00:46:32.519 --> 00:46:33.478
Where?

00:46:35.439 --> 00:46:36.648
Gyeong-nam, get in!

00:46:36.732 --> 00:46:38.317
-Je-gil!
-We need an ambulance!

00:46:38.400 --> 00:46:39.276
Open your eyes!

00:46:39.359 --> 00:46:40.402
-Lizard!
-Open your eyes!

00:46:44.156 --> 00:46:45.532
Go!

00:46:49.077 --> 00:46:51.288
You idiots! Go after them!

00:46:55.000 --> 00:46:56.752
-Mr. Park…
-You're okay.

00:46:56.835 --> 00:46:58.754
Breathe. Stay with me.

00:47:05.218 --> 00:47:07.429
Stay with me, Lizard.

00:47:07.929 --> 00:47:09.890
We're going to the hospital.
Hang in there.

00:47:09.973 --> 00:47:11.016
They used a knife?

00:47:12.351 --> 00:47:13.852
Am I bleeding a lot?

00:47:13.935 --> 00:47:16.647
Wait. Hold on. Blood…

00:47:16.730 --> 00:47:18.732
He's not bleeding.

00:47:19.232 --> 00:47:20.901
Can't you even tell? Look carefully.

00:47:20.984 --> 00:47:23.028
He really isn't bleeding.

00:47:23.111 --> 00:47:24.071
Lizard!

00:47:32.454 --> 00:47:34.164
I'm really thorough, you know.

00:47:34.247 --> 00:47:36.291
The car is so fancy,
the manual is thick as hell.

00:47:37.084 --> 00:47:38.835
Geez! You scared us to death!

00:47:38.919 --> 00:47:40.087
God, that scared me.

00:47:40.170 --> 00:47:41.129
What the heck?

00:47:42.964 --> 00:47:44.633
I'm a bit touched, though.

00:47:44.716 --> 00:47:47.219
I thought handsome guys like you
would be cold-blooded.

00:47:47.302 --> 00:47:50.263
"Lizard! Open your eyes!"

00:47:50.347 --> 00:47:52.766
"We're going to the hospital!
Stay with me! Open your eyes!"

00:47:52.849 --> 00:47:53.850
"Hang in there, Lizard!"

00:47:53.934 --> 00:47:55.602
"Keep breathing!"

00:47:56.186 --> 00:47:57.813
Hey, Lizard.

00:47:57.896 --> 00:47:59.564
Do you want to visit the rooftop again?

00:47:59.648 --> 00:48:01.149
I'm sorry… "Lizard!"

00:48:01.233 --> 00:48:03.402
"Open your eyes!
We're going to the hospital!"

00:48:03.485 --> 00:48:05.028
-"Stay with me, Lizard!"
-Geez.

00:48:05.112 --> 00:48:06.154
"Lizard!"

00:48:06.238 --> 00:48:08.490
We should go to the nearest rooftop, Boss.

00:48:16.748 --> 00:48:17.999
Should we

00:48:19.042 --> 00:48:20.544
head back now?

00:48:21.545 --> 00:48:23.922
Let's head back to our apartment complex.

00:48:24.005 --> 00:48:25.340
Not yet.

00:48:25.924 --> 00:48:26.967
Why not?

00:48:27.050 --> 00:48:30.387
No more trucks are coming out.
We've been waiting for a long time.

00:48:31.847 --> 00:48:33.348
Ms. Kang Ha-ri, you wait at the gate.

00:48:34.182 --> 00:48:35.726
If the other trucks are fake,

00:48:35.809 --> 00:48:38.437
the real one could come out last,
looking the least suspicious.

00:48:38.520 --> 00:48:40.355
If that's the case, follow that car.

00:48:52.284 --> 00:48:54.786
That one! It's the real one
Mr. Park was talking about!

00:48:56.705 --> 00:48:57.998
Goodness.

00:49:05.464 --> 00:49:06.923
Lee Chung-won!

00:49:07.007 --> 00:49:08.425
You saw that sly fox, right?

00:49:25.233 --> 00:49:26.318
Hey.

00:49:27.194 --> 00:49:30.155
Isn't this the way to True Value?

00:49:31.031 --> 00:49:33.533
All the other trucks were just bait.

00:49:33.617 --> 00:49:35.452
The real one was going to True Value.

00:49:36.453 --> 00:49:37.662
Oh my gosh.

00:49:54.971 --> 00:49:56.348
He's going in.

00:49:56.431 --> 00:49:57.933
He's entering the parking lot.

00:50:05.857 --> 00:50:06.942
DO NOT ENTER

00:50:07.025 --> 00:50:08.819
-Lower the window.
-What is this?

00:50:09.820 --> 00:50:12.155
Sir! Is there no one here?

00:50:12.239 --> 00:50:13.532
-Sir!
-I don't see anyone.

00:50:13.615 --> 00:50:15.867
-Hang on. I can't see.
-Darn it. We have to hurry.

00:50:17.869 --> 00:50:19.496
-Call them.
-Excuse me!

00:50:19.579 --> 00:50:21.122
Anyone there?

00:50:21.206 --> 00:50:22.374
Sir!

00:50:23.291 --> 00:50:24.543
So you mean

00:50:24.626 --> 00:50:27.879
the money went to one
of the 9,800 households?

00:50:27.963 --> 00:50:30.048
The odds are 1 in 9,800.

00:50:30.966 --> 00:50:32.384
That's too broad.

00:50:32.467 --> 00:50:35.720
The money came back
to our apartment complex.

00:50:35.804 --> 00:50:39.099
We'll find it even if we have
to press 9,800 doorbells.

00:50:39.182 --> 00:50:41.685
We don't have to look
through 9,800 households.

00:50:42.185 --> 00:50:44.646
We just have to find the one house

00:50:45.230 --> 00:50:48.233
that Lee Chung-won chose among them.

00:51:02.831 --> 00:51:04.708
What about Park Hae-kang?

00:51:04.791 --> 00:51:06.126
It's fine.

00:51:06.209 --> 00:51:09.379
Killing Park Hae-kang
wasn't our goal today.

00:51:09.462 --> 00:51:11.756
Our goal was to distract him.

00:51:13.091 --> 00:51:15.010
And the car in the parking lot?

00:51:15.093 --> 00:51:16.303
He won't be able to find it.

00:51:28.607 --> 00:51:29.983
This is so good.

00:51:42.037 --> 00:51:42.871
Nice.

00:51:51.755 --> 00:51:52.797
Damn it.

00:51:53.924 --> 00:51:55.383
I thought Lee Chung-won

00:51:55.467 --> 00:51:57.385
was our incinerator

00:51:57.469 --> 00:52:01.056
who cleaned up our messes
without leaving a trace.

00:52:01.139 --> 00:52:02.474
I did too.

00:52:02.557 --> 00:52:04.517
But he didn't get rid of our waste.

00:52:04.601 --> 00:52:07.687
He was collecting it
and even putting name tags on it.

00:52:10.690 --> 00:52:12.609
Let's get Hanmin to take over.

00:52:13.902 --> 00:52:15.111
All right.

00:52:18.657 --> 00:52:21.576
Sorry I'm late.
Your call was quite sudden…

00:52:21.660 --> 00:52:23.036
Commissioner.

00:52:24.245 --> 00:52:25.747
-Hello.
-Please sit.

00:52:29.918 --> 00:52:33.004
Commissioner, I'm curious about something.

00:52:33.088 --> 00:52:36.174
What do the police usually do
if a car accident

00:52:36.257 --> 00:52:38.760
causes a huge traffic jam?

00:52:39.511 --> 00:52:40.512
Pardon?

00:52:43.932 --> 00:52:46.434
We have the vehicles towed
and clear the scene quickly.

00:52:46.518 --> 00:52:48.520
That's right. You tow them.

00:52:48.603 --> 00:52:52.440
Lee Chung-won is like a truck
in a car accident right now.

00:52:52.524 --> 00:52:56.361
The control system's down,
and the body is huge,

00:52:57.362 --> 00:52:58.905
so it's completely blocking our path.

00:53:01.157 --> 00:53:02.283
What?

00:53:02.367 --> 00:53:04.369
You can tow him away,

00:53:05.495 --> 00:53:06.913
can't you?

00:53:18.174 --> 00:53:19.426
I understand.

00:53:20.218 --> 00:53:21.428
I'll follow protocol

00:53:22.387 --> 00:53:24.014
and take care of it quietly.

00:53:27.142 --> 00:53:29.102
Yes. Follow protocol.

00:53:32.605 --> 00:53:33.940
-Je-gil.
-Yes?

00:53:35.275 --> 00:53:36.276
No, wait.

00:53:40.739 --> 00:53:43.283
-You can see all the residents.
-Yes.

00:53:46.786 --> 00:53:48.121
Did you order something again?

00:53:48.204 --> 00:53:49.956
You need to eat to stay strong.

00:53:50.040 --> 00:53:52.834
I was feeling a bit down,
so I made some pancakes.

00:53:52.917 --> 00:53:57.088
Mr. Choi, I made
your favorite kimchi pancakes.

00:53:57.172 --> 00:53:59.090
-Thank you.
-Hello, President Jang.

00:54:00.925 --> 00:54:01.760
Oh my gosh.

00:54:02.510 --> 00:54:05.013
Ms. Kang, how are you here?

00:54:05.764 --> 00:54:07.390
Hello.

00:54:08.683 --> 00:54:13.021
You were hiding her here
and didn't tell me anything?

00:54:13.605 --> 00:54:16.691
We weren't hiding her.
We just thought she'd be the safest here.

00:54:17.358 --> 00:54:18.443
Oh my.

00:54:19.069 --> 00:54:21.071
I can't believe it.

00:54:21.154 --> 00:54:24.574
All of you are gathered here.

00:54:26.493 --> 00:54:29.662
I didn't even know you two were sisters.

00:54:29.746 --> 00:54:31.831
Looking at you now, you do look alike.

00:54:32.499 --> 00:54:36.002
But Ms. Kang,
you seem to have lost so much weight.

00:54:36.086 --> 00:54:37.378
Eat up.

00:54:37.462 --> 00:54:38.546
Thank you.

00:54:38.630 --> 00:54:43.384
But we have to find Lee Chung-won's vault
among 9,800 houses.

00:54:43.468 --> 00:54:44.928
Where could he have hidden it?

00:54:45.011 --> 00:54:46.262
The community center?

00:54:46.346 --> 00:54:48.681
Or some kind of storage room
we don't know about?

00:54:48.765 --> 00:54:49.641
Mr. Choi.

00:54:50.642 --> 00:54:53.228
There are too many people
visiting the community center,

00:54:53.311 --> 00:54:57.732
and the cleaning ladies
use the storage room several times a day.

00:54:57.816 --> 00:54:59.400
-He wouldn't use that.
-Hang on.

00:55:00.068 --> 00:55:01.903
Then wouldn't he hide it in his own house?

00:55:01.986 --> 00:55:05.448
The penthouse would be huge.

00:55:05.532 --> 00:55:08.618
But he'll get busted
as soon as a search warrant is issued.

00:55:08.701 --> 00:55:09.828
Then Mr. Choi.

00:55:09.911 --> 00:55:11.079
Yes, sir?

00:55:11.162 --> 00:55:13.289
There's no need to get up.

00:55:13.373 --> 00:55:15.750
You're making it look like
I'm really rude.

00:55:15.834 --> 00:55:16.793
Sorry, sir.

00:55:18.086 --> 00:55:22.507
Then doesn't Lee Chung-won
own any other units in True Value?

00:55:22.590 --> 00:55:24.050
Even under a different name?

00:55:26.803 --> 00:55:30.014
There aren't any on the list of owners.

00:55:30.098 --> 00:55:32.100
Then what about under Mr. Kim's name?

00:55:32.183 --> 00:55:34.102
There's no need.

00:55:34.936 --> 00:55:37.188
How about units
that were recently vacated?

00:55:37.856 --> 00:55:38.940
Even if they're not,

00:55:39.023 --> 00:55:42.402
units with unusually low
electricity or water usage.

00:55:42.986 --> 00:55:44.737
Can you check units like that?

00:55:46.030 --> 00:55:48.449
I know this unit. Unit 105.

00:55:48.533 --> 00:55:51.077
Their kids went to study abroad.

00:55:51.161 --> 00:55:52.871
That's why they're not home.

00:55:52.954 --> 00:55:55.790
And Building 307, Unit 1802.

00:55:55.874 --> 00:55:58.042
Gosh, Mr. Choi. Remember?

00:55:58.126 --> 00:56:02.088
They caused a huge scene
after the man cheated on his wife.

00:56:02.172 --> 00:56:03.506
The man left first,

00:56:03.590 --> 00:56:05.466
but the woman
doesn't come home these days.

00:56:05.550 --> 00:56:08.678
So they're both having an affair.
What about the kids?

00:56:08.761 --> 00:56:10.221
Then there are three houses left.

00:56:10.305 --> 00:56:11.681
If there are only three left,

00:56:11.764 --> 00:56:14.684
can't we just break into them
and check for ourselves?

00:56:14.767 --> 00:56:18.813
Hey, they're owned units.
You could get sued for breaking in.

00:56:18.897 --> 00:56:21.524
Wait. There's one more unit.

00:56:22.275 --> 00:56:24.986
The maintenance fee
is being paid automatically,

00:56:25.069 --> 00:56:27.697
but there hasn't been
any water usage the past month.

00:56:28.698 --> 00:56:29.949
Where is it?

00:56:32.035 --> 00:56:34.078
Unit 2903. Seo Gang-won's house.

00:56:50.553 --> 00:56:52.722
I got it in one go. Come on.

00:56:56.267 --> 00:56:58.519
Hey, Gyeong-nam.

00:56:58.603 --> 00:56:59.812
You actually got the passcode?

00:56:59.896 --> 00:57:01.731
-Be quiet.
-That's amazing.

00:57:01.814 --> 00:57:03.316
There's no one here.

00:57:06.236 --> 00:57:07.612
What is all that?

00:57:08.988 --> 00:57:10.114
This is crazy!

00:57:12.867 --> 00:57:13.910
What? Is this all cash?

00:57:13.993 --> 00:57:15.912
All of this is cash?

00:57:16.746 --> 00:57:18.122
This…

00:57:18.206 --> 00:57:19.040
No way!

00:57:21.125 --> 00:57:22.252
It's cash.

00:57:22.794 --> 00:57:24.212
We found Lee Chung-won's vault.

00:57:25.213 --> 00:57:26.923
I've never seen

00:57:27.006 --> 00:57:29.509
so much cash before in my life.

00:57:29.592 --> 00:57:31.803
He really does things
on a different scale.

00:57:31.886 --> 00:57:33.930
He sure is bold.

00:57:34.013 --> 00:57:36.140
But this seems to be
more than 17.8 billion.

00:57:36.224 --> 00:57:37.058
Really?

00:57:37.141 --> 00:57:40.395
He embezzled funds
from other apartment complexes too.

00:57:40.478 --> 00:57:42.730
He used it all as his personal fund.

00:57:42.814 --> 00:57:43.815
Oh my gosh.

00:57:43.898 --> 00:57:45.692
Then we…

00:57:45.775 --> 00:57:47.735
What do we do

00:57:47.819 --> 00:57:49.195
about all this money?

00:57:49.904 --> 00:57:51.990
We'll take our 17.8 billion

00:57:52.073 --> 00:57:54.576
and return the rest
to the other apartment complexes.

00:57:59.080 --> 00:58:00.373
What's with you?

00:58:01.040 --> 00:58:04.252
We need something
to stake our claim to this money.

00:58:04.335 --> 00:58:07.046
We should report it first, right?

00:58:07.130 --> 00:58:09.632
We need to take care of this legally.

00:58:09.716 --> 00:58:11.092
No.

00:58:11.175 --> 00:58:13.678
Lee Chung-won has connections
in the police too. It won't work.

00:58:13.761 --> 00:58:15.680
We might end up losing the money again.

00:58:15.763 --> 00:58:18.850
Lee Chung-won's name
isn't in the ledger my sister wrote.

00:58:18.933 --> 00:58:20.977
He'll easily get away with this.

00:58:21.060 --> 00:58:23.104
We'll lose if we go by the law.

00:58:24.731 --> 00:58:27.734
Then we can use this situation
to our advantage.

00:58:29.110 --> 00:58:30.236
How?

00:58:32.697 --> 00:58:34.782
Mr. Choi and Ms. Kang Ha-jeong
can take the blame.

00:58:34.866 --> 00:58:35.908
What?

00:58:36.701 --> 00:58:38.828
Right. That's a good idea.

00:58:39.704 --> 00:58:41.623
This is President Seo's house.

00:58:42.206 --> 00:58:43.166
You can say

00:58:43.249 --> 00:58:47.253
that the money you embezzled is here
and that you felt guilty,

00:58:47.337 --> 00:58:49.964
so you'd like to return
all the money you pocketed.

00:58:50.840 --> 00:58:53.217
Like a public confession?

00:58:53.301 --> 00:58:55.470
You should brace yourself.

00:58:55.553 --> 00:58:56.596
My gosh.

00:58:56.679 --> 00:58:58.765
Lee Chung-won
won't be able to claim that it's his.

00:58:58.848 --> 00:59:00.725
If he does, he'll become an embezzler

00:59:00.808 --> 00:59:03.227
and have to explain
President Seo's disappearance.

00:59:04.145 --> 00:59:05.146
Bravo.

00:59:05.229 --> 00:59:06.606
That's such a good idea.

00:59:06.689 --> 00:59:08.650
You're so smart.

00:59:08.733 --> 00:59:12.695
Let's reveal the 17.8 billion
to the residents first.

00:59:12.779 --> 00:59:14.280
We'll make the announcement

00:59:14.364 --> 00:59:17.158
that President Park
got our reserve fund back.

00:59:17.241 --> 00:59:19.285
-What do you think?
-That's good.

00:59:20.078 --> 00:59:24.457
We'll make all 9,800 households
our witnesses.

00:59:27.126 --> 00:59:31.714
I'm going to turn myself in
after we reveal the money tomorrow,

00:59:31.798 --> 00:59:33.174
as I promised.

00:59:34.425 --> 00:59:35.927
Don't be too scared.

00:59:39.180 --> 00:59:42.183
Thank you for everything so far.

00:59:42.266 --> 00:59:43.393
For protecting me.

00:59:45.728 --> 00:59:47.689
Once you're released,

00:59:47.772 --> 00:59:51.442
I'll be waiting with a cake,

00:59:51.526 --> 00:59:52.944
so hurry back.

00:59:54.904 --> 00:59:56.531
Cake? Not tofu?

00:59:57.490 --> 01:00:00.034
Well, I…

01:00:00.118 --> 01:00:02.620
I didn't trust women
after what happened with my ex-wife.

01:00:02.704 --> 01:00:06.124
But you're like an angel.

01:00:06.207 --> 01:00:09.836
I learned that
there are kind people like you too.

01:00:09.919 --> 01:00:12.463
I heard that you want
to become a patissier.

01:00:12.547 --> 01:00:15.633
So I thought you'd like it
if I got a cake for you instead.

01:00:15.717 --> 01:00:18.469
Well, I was just trying to flirt.

01:00:23.558 --> 01:00:26.310
I like mango cakes.

01:00:28.813 --> 01:00:29.814
Mango…

01:00:37.739 --> 01:00:39.866
"Hands in the air.
I'll shoot if you move."

01:00:39.949 --> 01:00:42.493
But then the woman raised her head,

01:00:42.577 --> 01:00:44.537
and her eyes weren't human.

01:00:44.620 --> 01:00:46.038
Isn't that scary?

01:00:48.374 --> 01:00:49.292
Hey.

01:00:51.169 --> 01:00:52.962
What's wrong, Big Guy?

01:00:53.045 --> 01:00:54.046
Big Guy.

01:00:57.842 --> 01:00:58.801
I'm cold!

01:01:00.553 --> 01:01:01.596
What's with you?

01:01:06.392 --> 01:01:07.226
Drink.

01:01:09.645 --> 01:01:13.357
You still have to face the consequences.

01:01:14.108 --> 01:01:16.694
But you've been very cooperative,

01:01:16.778 --> 01:01:20.573
so we'll submit petitions for leniency

01:01:20.656 --> 01:01:22.450
on your behalf.

01:01:25.036 --> 01:01:26.037
Thank you…

01:01:26.746 --> 01:01:27.663
so much.

01:01:29.624 --> 01:01:30.666
Drink up.

01:01:37.632 --> 01:01:39.091
Get some sleep.

01:01:39.175 --> 01:01:41.177
You look like your eyes
are about to pop out.

01:01:42.220 --> 01:01:43.554
I'm not sleepy.

01:01:45.848 --> 01:01:48.476
You need your strength for tomorrow.

01:01:49.018 --> 01:01:50.812
Want to lean on my shoulder?

01:01:50.895 --> 01:01:51.729
Here.

01:01:54.774 --> 01:01:55.900
Really?

01:02:02.406 --> 01:02:03.574
Gosh.

01:02:04.992 --> 01:02:08.246
You can end your date and head inside now.
I'll keep watch.

01:02:08.329 --> 01:02:09.872
-It's not like that!
-We weren't!

01:02:09.956 --> 01:02:12.083
Why are you yelling?

01:02:12.166 --> 01:02:14.752
I didn't see anything.

01:02:16.045 --> 01:02:17.505
We didn't do anything.

01:02:18.172 --> 01:02:20.967
You were all…

01:02:22.009 --> 01:02:22.844
What?

01:02:25.388 --> 01:02:27.306
What's wrong with you?

01:02:31.352 --> 01:02:33.271
Everything will be over tomorrow, right?

01:02:34.564 --> 01:02:38.109
I'm so excited to see
the look on Lee Chung-won's face.

01:02:38.192 --> 01:02:41.654
We have to make sure
he'll never be able to smile again.

01:02:42.321 --> 01:02:43.447
Never.

01:02:45.700 --> 01:02:48.661
And after everything's
wrapped up tomorrow,

01:02:48.744 --> 01:02:50.955
you should get back
to studying for the bar exam.

01:02:51.706 --> 01:02:53.624
I'll help you in your sister's place.

01:02:54.917 --> 01:02:56.335
We're family.

01:03:03.467 --> 01:03:04.385
Why?

01:03:07.013 --> 01:03:08.681
Why would you go that far?

01:03:09.932 --> 01:03:10.766
Can't you…

01:03:12.476 --> 01:03:14.562
just think of me as Daddy-Long-Legs?

01:03:15.521 --> 01:03:16.606
What?

01:03:16.689 --> 01:03:17.565
No way.

01:03:18.733 --> 01:03:19.859
What?

01:03:19.942 --> 01:03:23.070
That line was a bit cringe, you know.

01:03:23.154 --> 01:03:24.196
What do you mean?

01:03:25.156 --> 01:03:27.366
Daddy-Long-Legs is a good thing.

01:03:27.450 --> 01:03:29.535
-It's like a benefactor.
-Mr. Park.

01:03:29.619 --> 01:03:32.121
Don't you know the ending
of Daddy-Long-Legs?

01:03:32.204 --> 01:03:35.708
Judy Abbott ends up marrying
that Daddy-Long-Legs.

01:03:36.417 --> 01:03:37.501
They get married?

01:03:39.670 --> 01:03:43.883
Are you saying you'll make me
into Judy Abbott and try something funny?

01:03:44.634 --> 01:03:46.719
You're a scary man.

01:03:46.802 --> 01:03:47.762
I…

01:03:47.845 --> 01:03:49.430
That's not what I meant.

01:03:49.513 --> 01:03:51.849
Judy actually… Geez.

01:03:52.433 --> 01:03:54.018
This is bad, Ms. Kang!

01:03:55.394 --> 01:03:59.482
WE FOUND THE LOST 17.8 BILLION!

01:04:08.157 --> 01:04:09.575
I didn't know money was so heavy.

01:04:10.952 --> 01:04:13.329
Great job!

01:04:19.210 --> 01:04:22.713
All right, President Park.
You should say something.

01:04:23.422 --> 01:04:26.425
We couldn't have found it
without President Park.

01:04:26.509 --> 01:04:27.677
He's amazing.

01:04:27.760 --> 01:04:28.594
Right.

01:04:28.678 --> 01:04:31.347
I knew President Park
would be able to resolve this elegantly.

01:04:31.430 --> 01:04:34.475
Then we all helped
find the reserve fund, didn't we?

01:04:34.558 --> 01:04:36.268
-Of course!
-We did it together.

01:04:36.352 --> 01:04:39.563
Everyone, I'm at the True Value site.

01:04:39.647 --> 01:04:41.816
Do you see those apple boxes?

01:04:41.899 --> 01:04:44.777
They're actually filled with cash.
The real fund.

01:04:48.948 --> 01:04:51.575
Hello. I'm President Park Hae-kang.

01:04:54.662 --> 01:04:57.915
The reason why I asked you all
to gather here today

01:04:58.708 --> 01:05:01.085
is that our facility manager
and accounting manager

01:05:01.168 --> 01:05:03.629
decided to reveal
the location of the lost fund,

01:05:03.713 --> 01:05:06.132
and we've brought it all back.

01:05:09.135 --> 01:05:12.138
What's more, I wanted you all
to see the money in person

01:05:12.221 --> 01:05:14.181
to prevent unnecessary misunderstandings.

01:05:14.265 --> 01:05:15.099
Goodness.

01:05:15.182 --> 01:05:18.185
I'd like you to check our reserve fund
with your own eyes

01:05:18.269 --> 01:05:21.605
and keep showing your interest
in True Value's matters

01:05:21.689 --> 01:05:23.899
so this will never happen again.

01:05:23.983 --> 01:05:26.777
We'd like for every one of you
to be watchdogs of the community.

01:05:28.654 --> 01:05:31.365
-Watchdogs!
-Watchdogs!

01:05:31.449 --> 01:05:34.368
-Watchdogs!
-Watchdogs!

01:05:34.452 --> 01:05:36.871
-Watchdogs!
-Hey, come down.

01:05:37.705 --> 01:05:39.206
All right, everyone.

01:05:39.290 --> 01:05:41.375
I will now show you
True Value's reserve fund

01:05:41.459 --> 01:05:44.628
that we've gotten back
with your sacrifice and cooperation.

01:05:54.388 --> 01:05:56.432
All right. Here is your reserve…

01:05:57.433 --> 01:05:58.559
-Hurry up!
-What's he doing?

01:05:58.642 --> 01:06:00.311
Come on!

01:06:01.228 --> 01:06:02.855
-What's he doing?
-What is it?

01:06:09.153 --> 01:06:10.404
What is it?

01:06:10.488 --> 01:06:12.698
Stop messing around and show us.

01:06:18.245 --> 01:06:19.622
-What?
-What is that?

01:06:26.462 --> 01:06:28.214
What's going on?

01:06:34.804 --> 01:06:37.431
LIZARD

01:06:38.432 --> 01:06:41.268
Mr. Park, did you forget
that I'm the Lizard?

01:06:42.019 --> 01:06:45.189
Cutting off a tail is nothing to me.

01:06:45.272 --> 01:06:48.025
I'll take the money.

01:06:57.284 --> 01:06:58.744
Open the other boxes.

01:06:58.828 --> 01:07:00.412
Open the one next to it!

01:07:00.496 --> 01:07:01.872
That one too?

01:07:01.956 --> 01:07:03.749
What? What's going on?

01:07:03.833 --> 01:07:04.667
What's this?

01:07:05.709 --> 01:07:06.877
What is all this?

01:07:13.676 --> 01:07:15.761
I'm sure the money was in here.

01:07:30.651 --> 01:07:31.819
We got robbed again?

01:07:45.166 --> 01:07:52.131
Lizard!

01:07:58.220 --> 01:08:01.140
THE APARTMENT JOB

01:08:37.801 --> 01:08:39.803
Subtitle translation by: Juyoung Park